# Titan Orbit — Windows late-join (seed-hydrate)

> **Agents:** also read `titan-orbit-teamchoice-crash-hardstop.mdc`.
> Prefer `ClientJoinSettleCache.ShouldSkipShipEntityQueries` / `ShouldSkipMapBodyQueries`.

## Architecture (current)

| Layer | Contract |
|---|---|
| Recipe | `MapSessionMetaRpc` carries match **seed** + `MapGenerationConfig` + asteroid body tuning |
| Client map | `ClientMapHydrateSystem` Instantiates **local** asteroids from `MapLayoutBlueprint` (not GhostSpawn) |
| Relevancy | `TitanOrbitDynamicGhostRelevancySystem`: `SetIsRelevant` for Ship / Gem / PeopleTransport / **Planet** only |
| GoInGame | Client adds `NetworkStreamInGame` only after hydrate complete (+ GhostCollection) |
| Progress | Loading bar = seed hydrate progress, then short InGame catch-up — not Instantiates=1 of 700 rocks |
| Transform | `TransformSystemGroup` **ON** during play (session-long quarantine retired) |
| Ships | Still gate with `ShouldSkipShipEntityQueries` around TeamChoice Instantiates |

## Why Instantiates=1 / TransformQuarantine was retired

Those were Crash!!! workarounds for streaming every asteroid as a ghost. Seed-hydrate removes that Instantiates storm. Do **not** reintroduce asteroid relevancy “to simplify networking.”

## Absolute forbidden

1. Put `AsteroidTag` in DefaultRelevancyQuery under SetIsRelevant.
2. GoInGame before hydrate when `HasFullRecipe`.
3. Loading dismiss at 0 hydrated asteroids with a full recipe.
4. Ship gathers without `ShouldSkipShipEntityQueries`.
5. CreateEntity-cap+requeue leftovers in GhostSpawn (ghost-map hole).
6. Editing only Package Cache NetCode — patch lives in git `Packages/com.unity.netcode` + `tools/netcode-patches/`.

